<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jalisco</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jalisco is a state of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, with its capital at Guadalajara, the country's second-largest city. Its lands formed the core of the colonial kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-galicia">New Galicia</a>, conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nuno-de-guzman">Nuño de Guzmán</a> from 1529, and later the intendancy of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guadalajara-mexico">Guadalajara</a>. It became a state of the Mexican federation in 1823 and is known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of mariachi music and tequila.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jalisco.jpg" alt="Jalisco" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gobierno de Jalisco · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Jalisco.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
